# Every text file is LF on every checkout, including a checkout on Windows.
#
# Git for Windows writes CRLF by default. The corpus files of a grammar are
# compared byte for byte with the output of the parser, so a CR that git adds
# on checkout makes a test fail. Upstream tree-sitter and every grammar that
# its tool writes use the same rule. See dbmeta D89 and D110.
* text=auto eol=lf
